Subject: Fix incompatible function-pointer types in ext/zlib and main/php_scandir for Clang 16+
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Clang 16+ treats -Wincompatible-function-pointer-types as a hard error. While Zend/zend_API.h already casts globals constructors in ZEND_GINIT()/PHP_GINIT(), ext/zlib/zlib.c bypassed PHP_GINIT(zlib) and passed raw ZEND_MODULE_GLOBALS_CTOR_N(zlib) (type void (*)(zend_zlib_globals *) instead of void (*)(void *)) in php_zlib_module_entry; similarly main/php_scandir.c passed compare (const struct dirent **) directly to qsort() without casting to int (*)(const void *, const void *). Align both sites with upstream PHP 7.0.
Upstream-Status: Backport (fixed upstream in PHP 7.0 ext/zlib/zlib.c and main/php_scandir.c)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none
Origin-Kind: backport
Origin-Project: php/php-src
Origin-Commit: PHP-7.0.33
Origin-URL: https://github.com/php/php-src/tree/PHP-7.0.33

--- a/ext/zlib/zlib.c
+++ b/ext/zlib/zlib.c
@@ -1032,7 +1032,7 @@ zend_module_entry php_zlib_module_entry = {
 	PHP_MINFO(zlib),
 	"2.0",
 	PHP_MODULE_GLOBALS(zlib),
-	ZEND_MODULE_GLOBALS_CTOR_N(zlib),
+	PHP_GINIT(zlib),
 	NULL,
 	NULL,
 	STANDARD_MODULE_PROPERTIES_EX
--- a/main/php_scandir.c
+++ b/main/php_scandir.c
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ PHPAPI int php_scandir(const char *dirname, struct dirent **namelist[], int (*se
 	*namelist = vector;
 
 	if (compare) {
-		qsort (*namelist, nfiles, sizeof(struct dirent *), compare);
+		qsort (*namelist, nfiles, sizeof(struct dirent *), (int (*) (const void *, const void *)) compare);
 	}
 
 	return nfiles;
